  "prefLabel": "Bcr 210.01 Consolidation",
  "priorExpiration": "2012-07-16",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Bcr 210.01 Consolidation. Adjudicative proceedings which involve the same, or substantially related, issues shall be consolidated for hearing or decision, or both, when fairness, accuracy and efficiency would be served by such an action. Consolidation shall be ordered in response to a timely motion from a party or on the board's own initiative.\n\nSource. #8044, eff 2-17-04; ss by #10073, INTERIM, eff 1-17-12, EXPIRES: 7-16-12; ss by #10161, eff 7-13-12",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/bcr200.html"
